<title>GERMANY: Germany details tax estimates for 1997-1998. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>Germany details tax estimates for 1997-1998. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects table to show that changes are from previous estimate in November, not in May)</p>
<p>The German Finance Ministry gave the following data on expected tax revenues according to the latest half-year estimate by an official working group: (In billions of marks)</p>
<p>						1997     1998</p>
<p>Public sector (1)			 813.1    843.5</p>
<p>Change from Nov est.		    -18.0    -31.6</p>
<p>Breakdown by authority:  Federal    336.7    348.4</p>
<p>Change from Nov est.		    - 9.1    -14.6</p>
<p>States					337.1    349.8</p>
<p>Change from Nov est.		    - 6.9    -12.9</p>
<p>Local govts				  97.2    101.8</p>
<p>Change from Nov est.		    - 1.8    - 3.3</p>
<p>Transfers to EU			    42.1     43.4</p>
<p>Change from Nov est.		     -0.2     -0.7</p>
<p>NOTE - (1) Federal, state and local government tax revenues plus transfers to the European Union.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
